1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,200
Install tanstack-fetch. It is a tiny typed fetch client shaped for TanStack Query.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:11,200
createFetch builds a shared HTTP client. Methods return data directly — perfect for queryFn.

3
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:19,200
Handle 401 / 403 / 404 / 5xx before the error is thrown to TanStack Query.

4
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:27,700
Pass signal for cancellation. api.get<T>() resolves to T, or throws FetchError.

5
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:35,200
Mutations use body in options. Same client, same error model.

6
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:43,700
Wrap createFetch once. Apps only pass baseURL, auth, mocks, and status handlers.

7
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:51,700
Enable mocks for local/demo flows. Real network is used when mocks are off.

8
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:59,200
Same createFetch call path: controller → getApiClient().get → mock Response.json.

9
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:04,200
tanstack-fetch: typed fetch for TanStack Query — createFetch, status handlers, mocks, zero Axios.
